        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
         {
          "marks": [],
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Potential energy lost = 2.0 × 9.8 × 1.5 = 29.4 J. Kinetic energy gained = ½ × 2.0 × 4.0² = 16.0 J. Work done against friction = 29.4 − 16.0 = 13.4 J. Friction acts along the chute (5.0 m): "
         },
         {
          "marks": [],
          "type": "math_inline",
          "attrs": {
           "latex": "f"
          }
         },
         {
          "marks": [],
          "type": "text",
          "text": " = 13.4 / 5.0 = 2.7 N."
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
