         "marks": [],
         "type": "text",
         "text": "A diesel-powered pump raises water from a river to an irrigation tank. The water is raised through a vertical height of 18 m at a rate of 2.5 kg s⁻¹ and leaves the outlet pipe at the top with a speed of 4.0 m s⁻¹. The speed of the water in the river is negligible."
        }
